DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\\nCost: Fre
 e\\nAges: 0-60 months\\nCategory: Play & Games\\n\\nJoin us for a free eve
 ning where children and caretakers are invited to play in a sensory-friend
 ly\, neuro-affirming environment! We encourage the whole family to attend
 \, and therapists can join as well.\nNeurodivergent Family Nights are held
  on the second Tuesday and fourth Thursday of each month from 5-7 pm (afte
 r we close to general admission).\nOn these nights\, we dim the lights in 
 the museum\, turn off the sounds\, and offer a limited capacity of 250 gue
 sts. Staff are happy and ready to assist with providing various materials
 \, including noise-cancelling headphones\, fidget toys\, sunglasses\, and 
 weighted materials for your convenience.\nRSVP HERE\n*Registration is requ
 ired and opens two weeks before each event. \nPlay Partners TBD\\n\\nMore
  info: https://www.pretendcity.org/events/neurodivergent-family-night-4-20
 26-09-08/
