DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\\nAges: 0-6
 0 months\\nCategory: Music & Dance\\n\\nJoin us for Sustainable Saturdays 
 in partnership with Niagara Cares. Families can create art using recycled 
 materials while exploring fun ways to reuse everyday items. Together\, we&
 #8217\;ll learn how small changes can help care for our community and th
 e environment.\nIncluded in museum admission. Space is limited! Book you
 r tickets now.\n*Members do not require a reservation.\n*Events and dates 
 are subject to change.\nAbout the play partner: \nNiagara Cares is the he
 art of what we do and who we are at Niagara Bottling. For more than 60 yea
 rs\, we have been making a difference for our Team Members\, consumers and
  communities through philanthropic giving\, volunteering\, water donations
 \, and disaster relief. As a family-owned business\, we are committed to c
 reating meaningful change for our communities through a spirit of giving b
 ack both big and small. For more information\, visitniagarawater.com/niaga
 ra-cares.\nFrequently Asked Questions:\nIs Sustainable Saturdays included 
 with museum admission?\nYes. All Sustainable Saturdays activities are in
 cluded with regular museum admission. \nWhen does Sustainable Saturdays
  take place?\nSustainable Saturdays is held on the fourth Saturday of e
 very month in the Art Studio. \n&nbsp\;\n&nbsp\;\n&nbsp\;\n&nbsp\;\\n\\n
 More info: https://www.pretendcity.org/events/sustainable-saturdays/2026-0
 9-26/
